# The R3 board export (docs/r3/boards/) is an archival record: banked verbatim from Design's
# zip and verified by sha256, file by file. Its bytes ARE the artifact, so no filter may touch
# them. Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which smudges LF->CRLF on
# checkout — the stored blobs stay byte-correct, but a Windows working copy would not match
# the banked hashes.
#
# The hazard is the asymmetry, not the mismatch: a Linux clone hashes 26/26 green while a
# Windows clone shows 23 text files failing. Someone reading those failures as corruption
# could "repair" them by committing CRLF blobs, which would destroy the verbatim record for
# real while looking like housekeeping. This rule makes both platforms agree.
#
# Deliberately narrow. It pins ONE path, whose bytes are the point, and leaves diffs working
# normally. Do NOT widen it to `*` on a tidy-up: repo-wide normalisation would rewrite app
# code line endings, which is a separate decision with its own churn and no bearing on
# archiving a design export.
docs/r3/boards/** -text
